@startuml Arrival
title How a new picture comes on screen

' The pane's own state machine (arrival.rs beside this file). Each
' transition the pane takes in its tests is written to a trace and held
' against this diagram by Omaspec's trace check (docs/adr/0030).

state "Still" as Still : the picture on screen stands
state "Coming" as Coming : a new diagram is drawn; the picture on\nscreen stays as it was until the new one's\noverview is rasterized
state "Sheets" as Sheets : the overview is in; the sheets of parts\nof both pictures are on their way
state "Fading" as Fading : one picture fades into the other
state "Gliding" as Gliding {
  state "Alone" as Alone : nothing newer is drawn
  state "Following" as Following : a newer diagram is drawn; it waits\nfor its overview, then for the glide
  state "Waiting" as Waiting : its overview is in; the glide ends first
  [*] --> Alone
  Alone --> Following : drawn
  Following --> Following : drawn
  Following --> Waiting : overview
  Waiting --> Following : drawn
  Following --> Alone : no overview
  Waiting --> Alone : no overview
}

[*] --> Still
Still --> Coming : drawn
Coming --> Coming : drawn
Coming --> Still : no overview
Coming --> Fading : overview [it fades]
Coming --> Sheets : overview [it glides]
Sheets --> Sheets : overview [it glides]
Sheets --> Fading : overview [it fades after all]
Sheets --> Sheets : sheet [the other to come]
Sheets --> Gliding : sheet [both in]
Sheets --> Fading : sheet [it fades after all]
Sheets --> Fading : no sheet
Sheets --> Coming : drawn
Sheets --> Still : no overview
Fading --> Coming : drawn
Fading --> Still : faded
Alone --> Still : faded
Following --> Coming : faded
Waiting --> Fading : faded [it fades]
Waiting --> Sheets : faded [it glides]
Coming --> Still : released
Sheets --> Still : released
Fading --> Still : released
Gliding --> Still : released
@enduml
